      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Revolutionary War veterans like the Johnsons and Gash families settled here, building homesteads that still echo in the air.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://horseshoenc.us/about/history/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After the Civil War, freed families founded Shaw’s Creek AME Zion Church, the county’s first African‑American church, under trees near the campground.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
